# Run by openbox-session at login (the account is logged in by lightdm).
# Retrobox runs in the background: if it ends, Openbox stays up, with xterm in
# its right-click menu.
# The compositor first: vsync (no tearing) and the overlay's translucency over
# a game. GLX backend (NVIDIA's L4T driver). Without a config file
# (/etc/xdg/picom.conf turns on shadows and fades, which a console does not
# want): only vsync and compositing.
picom -b --config /dev/null --backend glx --vsync
retrobox &
